DESCRIPTION:For Employment and Job resources available from the Berkeley C
 ounty Library System\, see: Resume and Job Search Collection \n\nThe libra
 ry has computers\, printing\, copying\, faxing\, WiFi\, and more!\n\nCheck
  out FREE library resources such as Linkedin Learning to learn a new skill
 \, take a refresher course\, or earn a certificate!\nUnlimited Access | Mo
 re than 6\,000  video tutorials covering business\, creative\, and technol
 ogy topics.\n\nVisit jobs.scworks.org to log in or create an account to le
 arn more about a job you’re interested in.  \n\nEnter the Job Order # to
  search for jobs. For additional assistance\, please visit your local SC W
 orks center.\n\nSC Works Employment and Workforce: Veterans Day Career Fai
 r!\n\nIn honor of Veterans Day\, SC Works Trident in partnership with Trid
 ent Technical College\, are hosting a dedicated Veterans Day Career Fair t
 o connect our military community with local employers looking to hire top 
 talent.\n\nWhether you are a veteran\, transitioning from service\, Nation
 al Guard/Reserve member\, military spouse\, or a jobseeker and supporter o
 f our veterans\, this event offers a direct opportunity to network\, inter
 view\, and expore meaningful career opportunities.\n\nWhen:\n\nTuesday\, N
 ovember 10th\, 2026\n\n➤ Veterans & Military Spouses: 10:00 A.M. – 10:
 30 A.M.\n\n➤ General Public: 10:30 A.M. – 1:00 P.M.\n\nWhere: \n\nTrid
 ent Technical College Thornley Campus  \n7000 Rivers Avenue\, Building 410
 \, 2nd Floor\nNorth Charleston\, SC 29406\n\nSee participating employers a
 nd more details about the event HERE!\n\nBring multiple copies of your res
 ume & speak with recruiters hiring now across Berkeley\, Charleston and Do
 rchester County.\n\nParticipating Employers\n\n*Click one of the employers
  or partners below for job details and more information.\n\n\n	Beekmok Hos
 pitality Collection\n	Charleston County EMS\n	Charleston Water System\n	Co
 llege of Charleston\n	Detyens Shipyard\, Inc.\n	Home Instead\n	Keel\n	Newp
 ort News Shipbuilding\n	Schnellecke Logistics\n	Sea Island Land Developmen
 t\n	SignaPay Southeast\n	The Citadel\, The Military College of South Carol
 ina\n\n\nParticipating Partners & Resources\n\n\n	Operation Palmetto Emplo
 yment\n	The Charleston Vet Center\n	Trident Technical College\n\n\nThis ev
 ent is open to the public.\n\n
